Subject: TacetOS line in the info file

The info file of every build gets one more line, "TacetOS: <version>", after
the version of the base. The app reads it to tell a TacetOS firmware from
another build of the same base, and to compare its version with the one of the
update channel. The version comes from the environment variable
TACETOS_VERSION, which build.sh sets; a build without it writes no such line.

diff --git a/tools/mkinfo.pl b/tools/mkinfo.pl
index 463a100..42e30af 100755
--- a/tools/mkinfo.pl
+++ b/tools/mkinfo.pl
@@ -101,6 +101,11 @@ printf O ("Manufacturer: %s\n", $ENV{'MANUFACTURER'});
 # Variables identifying Rockbox and bootloader properties. Possibly changing
 # every software upgrade.
 printf O ("Version: %s", `$ENV{TOOLSDIR}/version.sh $ENV{ROOTDIR}`);
+# The TacetOS build names itself and gives its own version, which its build
+# script passes in. A build without it has no such line.
+if (defined $ENV{'TACETOS_VERSION'} && $ENV{'TACETOS_VERSION'} ne '') {
+    printf O ("TacetOS: %s\n", $ENV{'TACETOS_VERSION'});
+}
 printf O ("Binary: %s\n", $ENV{'BINARY'});
 printf O ("Binary size: %s\n", filesize($ENV{'BINARY'}));
 printf O ("Voice format: %s\n", definescan("$ENV{APPSDIR}/talk.h", "VOICE_VERSION"));
